ring_syntax_pitfalls_session.md_c4
[Syntax Pitfalls & Style 3 Traps > ## 3. Brace-style `if/else`: `else` goes INSIDE the closing `}`]

`if cond { ... } else { ... }` → R24 "Using uninitialized variable: else" (the `}` before
`else` detaches it from the `if`). CORRECT — `else`/`elseif`/`but` stay inside the braces:
```ring
# WRONG (R24):
if len(aArgs) >= 3 {
    cOutput = aArgs[3]
} else {
    cOutput = "default.txt"
}
# CORRECT:
if len(aArgs) >= 3 {
    cOutput = aArgs[3]
else
    cOutput = "default.txt"
}
```


